#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:5
msgid "Safe `fs.ReadStream` and `fs.WriteStream` using the same fd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Let's say that you want to perform a parallel upload of a file to a "
"remote server. To do this, we want to create multiple read streams. The "
"first thing you might think of is to use the `{start: 0, end: 0}` API of "
"`fs.createReadStream`. This gives you two choices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:12
msgid "Use the same file descriptor for all `fs.ReadStream` objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:13
msgid ""
"Open the file multiple times, resulting in a separate file descriptor for"
" each read stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:16
msgid ""
"Neither of these are acceptable options. The first one is a severe bug, "
"because the API docs for `fs.write` state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:19
msgid ""
"Note that it is unsafe to use `fs.write` multiple times on the same file "
"without waiting for the callback. For this scenario, "
"`fs.createWriteStream` is strongly recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:23
msgid ""
"`fs.createWriteStream` will solve the problem if you only create one of "
"them for the file descriptor, but it will exhibit this unsafety if you "
"create multiple write streams per file descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:27
msgid ""
"The second option suffers from a race condition. For each additional time"
" the file is opened after the first, it is possible that the file is "
"modified. So in our parallel uploading example, we might upload a corrupt"
" file that never existed on the client's computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:32
msgid ""
"This module solves this problem by providing `createReadStream` and "
"`createWriteStream` that operate on a shared file descriptor and provides"
" the convenient stream API while still allowing slicing and dicing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:36
msgid ""
"This module also gives you some additional power that the builtin "
"`fs.createWriteStream` do not give you. These features are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:39
msgid "Emitting a 'progress' event on write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:40
msgid "Ability to set a maximum size and emit an error if this size is exceeded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:41
msgid ""
"Ability to create an `FdSlicer` instance from a `Buffer`. This enables "
"you to provide API for handling files as well as buffers using the same "
"API."
msgstr ""

