#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:77
msgid "fdSlicer.createFromFd(fd, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:88
msgid ""
"Make sure `fd` is a properly initialized file descriptor. If you want to "
"use `createReadStream` make sure you open it for reading and if you want "
"to use `createWriteStream` make sure you open it for writing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:92 ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:107
msgid "`options` is an optional object which can contain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:94
msgid ""
"`autoClose` - if set to `true`, the file descriptor will be automatically"
" closed once the last stream that references it is closed. Defaults to "
"`false`. `ref()` and `unref()` can be used to increase or decrease the "
"reference count, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:99
msgid "fdSlicer.createFromBuffer(buffer, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:109
msgid ""
"`maxChunkSize` - A `Number` of bytes. see `createReadStream()`. If "
"falsey, defaults to unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:112
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:114
msgid "fd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:116
msgid "The file descriptor passed in. `undefined` if created from a buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:118
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:120
msgid "createReadStream(options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:122 ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:148
msgid "Available `options`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:124
msgid ""
"`start` - Number. The offset into the file to start reading from. "
"Defaults to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:126
msgid ""
"`end` - Number. Exclusive upper bound offset into the file to stop "
"reading from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:128
msgid ""
"`highWaterMark` - Number. The maximum number of bytes to store in the "
"internal buffer before ceasing to read from the underlying resource. "
"Defaults to 16 KB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:131
msgid ""
"`encoding` - String. If specified, then buffers will be decoded to "
"strings using the specified encoding. Defaults to `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:134
msgid "The ReadableStream that this returns has these additional methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:136
msgid ""
"`destroy(err)` - stop streaming. `err` is optional and is the error that "
"will be emitted in order to cause the streaming to stop. Defaults to `new"
" Error(\"stream destroyed\")`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:140
msgid ""
"If `maxChunkSize` was specified (see `createFromBuffer()`), the read "
"stream will provide chunks of at most that size. Normally, the read "
"stream provides the entire range requested in a single chunk, but this "
"can cause performance problems in some circumstances. See "
"[thejoshwolfe/yauzl#87](https://github.com/thejoshwolfe/yauzl/issues/87)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:146
msgid "createWriteStream(options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:150
msgid ""
"`start` - Number. The offset into the file to start writing to. Defaults "
"to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:152
msgid ""
"`end` - Number. Exclusive upper bound offset into the file. If this "
"offset is reached, the write stream will emit an 'error' event and stop "
"functioning. In this situation, `err.code === 'ETOOBIG'`. Defaults to "
"`Infinity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:155
msgid ""
"`highWaterMark` - Number. Buffer level when `write()` starts returning "
"false. Defaults to 16KB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:157
msgid ""
"`decodeStrings` - Boolean. Whether or not to decode strings into Buffers "
"before passing them to` _write()`. Defaults to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:160
msgid "The WritableStream that this returns has these additional methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:162
msgid "`destroy()` - stop streaming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:164
msgid "And these additional properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:166
msgid "`bytesWritten` - number of bytes written to the stream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:168
msgid "And these additional events:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:170
msgid "'progress' - emitted when `bytesWritten` changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:172
msgid "read(buffer, offset, length, position, callback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:174
msgid ""
"Equivalent to `fs.read`, but with concurrency protection. `callback` must"
" be defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:177
msgid "write(buffer, offset, length, position, callback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:179
msgid ""
"Equivalent to `fs.write`, but with concurrency protection. `callback` "
"must be defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:182
msgid "ref()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:184
msgid "Increase the `autoClose` reference count by 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:186
msgid "unref()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:188
msgid "Decrease the `autoClose` reference count by 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:190
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:192
msgid "'error'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:194
msgid "Emitted if `fs.close` returns an error when auto closing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:196
msgid "'close'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fd-slicer_README.md:198
msgid ""
"Emitted when fd-slicer closes the file descriptor due to `autoClose`. "
"Never emitted if created from a buffer."
msgstr ""

